# goat_fight (kenshi-h2v.29.28). A weak animal that our side can kill: one wild Goat on beak_open_ground's open ground against a six-character
# player squad (a lone Wanderer loses at once: the goat's chest hit takes 96 to -35 and downs him, kenshi-h2v.29.28's first run). The creature voices
# (VO_Creature_Take_Damage / VO_Creature_Die) need an animal that takes hits and dies; the Beak Thing of beak_open_ground downs the Wanderer at once, so
# nothing ever hits it. Goat: RACE 'Goat' (rebirth.mod `sounds` 10 -> Creature_VO "Goat", characters.cpp voiceOf: kCreature[sounds - 4]), the weakest
# animal record. FACTION 'Wildlife' hostile=1 so the fight is a real one. Only the player is ever ordered (docs/reference/SCENARIO_IMPORT.md "Rule").
# Every player wears Mercenary Plate (`item ... sid=2148-gamedata.base section=shirt`): without it the goat's 29 cut / 16 stun hit downs a character.
# What it takes to kill an animal here (kenshi-h2v.29.28's runs): bare fists deal BLUNT only (`hit: 41260 ... damage 0.0 1.9 0.0`), which costs no
# blood, so 31 landed hits over 132 s left the goat standing (it heals at 0.3 blood/s whenever it is not bleeding). Katanas (`476-gamedata.base`)
# land 22 cut a hit but down it first: a KO body is not a target (combat.cpp, task BK), and death needs `blood < -maxBlood` (combat_rules.cpp
# updateBleeding). So the goat is a badly wounded animal (`bleeding=2`, the save's medical key in SCENARIO_IMPORT.md): the squad hits it, it goes
# down and bleeds out ~17 s in, and the sim's death event reaches the client as VO_Creature_Die.
KSCEN 2
scenario title=A%20goat%20on%20the%20road setup=Six%20Wanderer-squad%20characters%20on%20open%20ground%20with%20a%20wild%20Goat%20a%20few%20steps%20off%2C%20hostile. look_for=Attack%20the%20goat%3A%20does%20it%20take%20hits%20(creature%20voice)%20and%20die%20(creature%20death%20voice)%3F bead=kenshi-h2v.29.28 metrics=bodies_down,fight_s
